db/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377578 1111 #uuid "9b61b221-7945-56a8-a7b3-73079c4f6a00" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377579 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/26e4af1684065b2127b0d9ec33632128f62a3b2b3aa772b48062ed23708b1b7d.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377579 1111 #uuid "e554ab89-fe7f-525c-a846-c2ba8f101ed4" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377580 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377580 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377580 1111 #uuid "61bb293f-db50-51ad-8829-bbcc5891e87d" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377581 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/2f3d6fcce069f0b7b7918481b4cda68ba16fbb94dbf3ebe6b6841256470b84ea.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377581 1111 #uuid "358f5fbe-368e-5711-a698-a5048cca05c6" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377583 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1089 "q-181306" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,1]\\times {-1,1}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1113 #uuid "734eb671-4f30-5ac2-952a-94e297467ed9" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377582 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[-1,1]\\times {-1,1}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1],\\,y\\in {-1,1}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/3ed05ffc58aad1a6c75e7862c1175f497fb14870e6650cc6c4ce01c3df091d8b.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/0f57920b2532177b0d64ac3dc95feb6a476bb385112d736d702895862e7de2b2.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377584 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377585 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377586 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377587 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377588 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377584 13194139535976 true] [17592186377583 1110 #uuid "5b16d8bf-f59d-50e9-95b1-ca63b493d122" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377584 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377584 1111 #uuid "4776dbc6-8794-5c53-a8cb-80404fd745e3" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377585 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/c28ba6b0da8364f4e7f157b58827384f9e138a2c0fc53558ce7ab2df2f646747.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377585 1111 #uuid "19536bf3-d230-5da5-8b8a-4713f5008d48" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377586 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/82f9ecf98b8b2b4e5f75b3130e8483354c93922dc3a942e271562ac1ad17438e.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377586 1111 #uuid "67be282f-bb45-5a62-95a9-0e246e6b2d79" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377587 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/e0fa3e717af02a353db77ae8b357dc338c975166fb5fbe6c5c1309d1c1f511f2.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377587 1111 #uuid "dc04add8-f9fb-5bc0-94b6-32dfcedf6172" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377588 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/2922ff5e3a32e01fbc292898c88c1d8eca8d933897d4b9d3c1694b6f5cbeb2a2.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377588 1111 #uuid "4791ff23-185c-55c8-85f2-c7c4c028023c" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377590 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1089 "q-181775" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1113 #uuid "08ecacda-324b-5560-9b50-f8f610c3a69d" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377589 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377591 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377592 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377593 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377594 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377595 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377592 13194139535976 true] [17592186377590 1110 #uuid "4b6af7b2-85bf-5d28-a4af-4ace88731227" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377591 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/6bc02e0957ea0099329b8266d4960b542d86c19f44b4fc811ba0752512def666.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377591 1111 #uuid "c5242b65-0dd2-5811-a2fd-83d8b6a9fbb5" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377592 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377592 1111 #uuid "6a9f2766-9176-565e-9005-86cb985c3513" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377593 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/0f219c170d7e73a8a5c3d11afabe6763e25ade77be9ed8a0b7495a8d9f6be90c.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377593 1111 #uuid "90a904db-08a8-578e-9537-9af867244366" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377594 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4233644fb8c5e19f379fdbc001951869fd5d9062e1f14d0abbb53d677780fb0a.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377594 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377594 1111 #uuid "4640f671-87ff-5b8c-be17-90e5c65324c0" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377595 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/91f80f30887e5233d12ee814c1e991f81613bd52c9afd7334397b123b68b8bc7.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377595 1111 #uuid "4761020c-b561-5f0b-9113-5dde8b234e98" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377597 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1089 "q-181959" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1113 #uuid "9854e016-8489-5582-ad5c-ffa3a5b6e5ec" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377596 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times Z\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/179fdaa3921cb29f2d25ff97bce262fd13fb2ff591c12e97a33953e95967f6fc.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/7399e42988df8a809013393d8873b6a6e5f60b64c0419eadd7bb3c334eb410d6.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times Z$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377598 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377599 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377600 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377601 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377602 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377601 13194139535976 true] [17592186377597 1110 #uuid "d9585d6a-5e2c-5083-80c8-10c8741648f3" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377598 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/9b6a2c5b3c9fdded8d615980df00228e2637515af0a23f62ae58b891bec3e3e7.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377598 1111 #uuid "7a3826d3-f08b-53ed-88ec-78f9962aecbd" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377599 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/c9adb78f087651508a43514756abbc45170766d6bb14a069053c4bf71e78e0a3.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377599 1111 #uuid "10ad5c19-eb2d-58b4-a40a-07bf5e268d01" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377600 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/a1b02e904c1df760f47d623d3ff17538c284d7ef6125b786165113a383c79c3c.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377600 1111 #uuid "fafb19bb-f0f0-509b-8925-949bfdddb96b" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377601 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377601 1111 #uuid "4707e5bb-ac4f-5c30-a615-39865fdd5334" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377602 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/d42f10aac16e2c7405fbf158dacb1b46137cc03800f8660d0ff4cfe11c9edc63.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377602 1111 #uuid "7fee0fbf-dbb3-55f5-befc-a5d36eca3788" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377604 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1089 "q-181968" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1113 #uuid "6bae802a-d591-53eb-b628-21b012d03cee" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377603 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/8e6816767cd2010fca1b8991ed9c5e0c42d3a6d6466d78025534bc8362a174b9.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}={(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4d0fe261e790520e6a8786e6f024d5b9cb7cd54c18242103a1f4b77f09653abc.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377605 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377606 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377607 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377608 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377609 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377609 13194139535976 true] [17592186377604 1110 #uuid "3df13d12-44e0-549e-861d-8aba8be0e35f" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377605 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377605 1111 #uuid "c68e871a-0a82-58bb-b642-5b68d643546d" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377606 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/5888cf137eea674995b4c9cc37285b4130df5de3a2a2fa63b1b5b195910526c1.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377606 1111 #uuid "78d5da05-0d63-5c07-bacb-f6a347d15b54" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377607 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/2f28e6f8c8e6e9fa13b5285e25e5460d26548ffd9d71077d1c6073e6c4c743a1.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377607 1111 #uuid "e0d00a18-7602-5260-b18f-fbc3c13ece33" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377608 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/463ae2387423a48dd557af8cfd9b01b6bc08b95f1b3c2f337c6b0c53d3731fa2.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377608 1111 #uuid "49fb9617-3199-5b83-af26-fe562937296b" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377609 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377609 1111 #uuid "5c7d3cf6-9fe1-5fbd-bd15-f1bbe958cfe9" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377611 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1089 "q-184489" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1100 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={-1,2}\\times {-3,1}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1113 #uuid "659e44f3-afb3-574d-a533-7467d2366762" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377610 1145 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing ${-1,2}\\times {-3,1}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS={(-1,-3),(-1,1),(2,-3),(2,1)}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/09b74d8a7baf8c22cab4ad3841e53c7286cd72dd7523916544ea370595b199a9.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377612 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377613 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377614 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377615 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377616 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377612 13194139535976 true] [17592186377611 1110 #uuid "f807b770-75a0-567c-bfe2-245468d1f71b" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377612 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/09b74d8a7baf8c22cab4ad3841e53c7286cd72dd7523916544ea370595b199a9.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377612 1111 #uuid "410c6fde-0f9c-562f-ad13-272cad98373f" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377613 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/70f7c02b3bca2b816858eaef766b5bbf3ced8d8abf101ef38ecda19b73781ee3.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377613 1111 #uuid "3c78f06c-f6d2-516b-9bfd-0376e1048cea" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377614 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/aa3411e662566a609de5163269dbc1e7c0ad92f415b52936c5ef568d7058d2d2.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377614 1111 #uuid "e1d27bae-db90-55d7-9e7c-0890fb3a01e1" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377615 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/2eec72a5444533c1bb4f86836cf8479b76ae38d69c35f5f5eef5fd313a2365f0.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377615 1111 #uuid "3873d6f6-5e99-5129-afc6-d3a38b2c46ef" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377616 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/01d87db018bcbbf013d7f33519418849fe70e0d772870335482a7b07cfc89fd9.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377616 1111 #uuid "7282a5a4-444b-5044-bdd7-c10dda9f7356" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377618 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1089 "q-184506" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1100 "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}={i}\\times [-i,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1113 #uuid "781c20e7-0cf2-5b84-94ac-d0ecc8cce115" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377617 1145 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}={1}\\times [-1,1]={(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,-1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/f26fa8a525806370f5505ad097ead2b289192bb3a6eb3e341eb7c2f91a03531f.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [-i,i]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,-i)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/bfeafe4c3b800b33b4f8550de02c2eb908effb5c28ef59b40f8c5e2bcad38ac4.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377619 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377620 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377621 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377622 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377623 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377623 13194139535976 true] [17592186377618 1110 #uuid "e7bc1c81-08a7-5866-b655-e5a6a758afc6" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377619 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/e1d3407dfca8c57d9b7c14431260d91ec1fd60e312ecd2846026e0667a421cf2.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377619 1111 #uuid "fac6dfed-4dd7-507c-80c9-5a4056b8b7d1" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377620 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/ee6257f32003e385616c0e1f57f76ae9e9c23fd09f7348202a8f26433ac24056.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377620 1111 #uuid "65fe61b5-50bf-5966-9d2e-c980be53f702" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377621 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/e460699a3844c0e295af363760cdb8d4ce9ad54bc00c051ca517e4b7614db982.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377621 1111 #uuid "939248e0-50df-5dd8-95e3-ca90965242e3" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377622 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/0ff3c422678e1cb1c68a60f4957620e338095aa349f274338909886c2e6ed1e0.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377622 1111 #uuid "a3e175ed-932b-5c22-b2f5-c30bd88c1c1c" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377623 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377623 1111 #uuid "830b9fc3-8674-5c96-be78-a32467f1532f" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377625 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1089 "q-184508" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1100 "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-2i,2i]\\times [-i,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1113 #uuid "aaaa0132-50ce-55c2-8cb3-cf438d123c79" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377624 1145 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-1,1]\\times [-0.5,0.5]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-0.5,0.5]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(-1,-0.5),$ $(-1,0.5),$ $(1,0.5),$ and $(1,-0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/0a3f27ff85f8a5b56e912f33976846b36fc90d35a87201c146c5345f4e31ba46.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-2i,2i]\\times [-i,i]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-2i,2i],b\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(-2i,-i),$ $(-2i,i),$ $(2i,i),$ and $(2i,-i).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/d32279c2279fe234accaae96e5abc86a122adf60dc930c5e299b2f0c2db0028e.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the point $(0,0):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4fdd8fc71b47304bb87e2d70a229bc0a545f85f0fe268d79036884421ed3765e.png)" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377626 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377627 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377628 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377629 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377630 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1041 "selection" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377626 13194139535976 true] [17592186377625 1110 #uuid "d1a6bcdb-a9a8-5352-a137-8b9882c90d08" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377626 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4fdd8fc71b47304bb87e2d70a229bc0a545f85f0fe268d79036884421ed3765e.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377626 1111 #uuid "c433a444-dab5-5cba-a2b4-737de2569c74" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377627 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/456350246eb5d24142f2b53258bb20fa0c74ad377e90d23ce340b8883d8b418a.png" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535976 true] [17592186377627 1111 #uuid "d6e0847d-48c2-52b2-9c3f-79d2f7455a98" 13194139535976 true] [17592186377628 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/e59f8125b6d